{'query': 'reputable peer-reviewed scientific source on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'Causes and Effects of Climate Change | United Nations', 'url': 'https://www.un.org/en/climatechange/science/causes-effects-climate-change', 'snippet': 'This leads to global warming and climate change. The world is now warming faster than at any point in recorded history. Warmer temperatures over time are changing weather patterns and disrupting the usual balance of nature.'}, {'title': 'Causes of Climate Change | US EPA', 'url': 'https://www.epa.gov/climatechange-science/causes-climate-change', 'snippet': 'Causes of Climate Change. Natural processes are always influencing the earth’s climate and can explain climate changes prior to the Industrial Revolution in the 1700s.'}, {'title': 'Climate Change - NASA Science', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'What are the effects of climate change? The effects of human-caused global warming are happening now, are irreversible for people alive today, and will worsen as long as humans add greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.'}, {'title': 'What are the effects of global warming? | National Geographic', 'url': 'https://www.nationalgeographic.com/environment/article/global-warming-effects', 'snippet': 'Global warming and climate change are often used interchangeably as synonyms, but scientists prefer to use “climate change” when describing the complex shifts now affecting our planet’s weather and climate systems.'}, {'title': 'Climate fearmongering reaches stratospheric... - Watts Up With That?', 'url': 'https://wattsupwiththat.com/2023/06/05/climate-fearmongering-reaches-stratospheric-heights/', 'snippet': 'Is that considered a reputable peer reviewed journal? Just curious- the topic is way over my head.I suspect most of the climate alarmists have never experienced a lengthy pull in cold temperatures at night with no heat source except themselves. I have, several times.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 8.950686099997256}
{'query': 'government or international body report on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'Environmental issues - Wikipedia', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_issues', 'snippet': 'Water pollution is an environmental issue that affects many water bodies. This photograph shows foam on the New River as it enters the United States from Mexico.The 2023 IPCC report highlighted the disproportionate effects of climate change on vulnerable populations.'}, {'title': 'Climate Change | United Nations', 'url': 'https://www.un.org/en/global-issues/climate-change', 'snippet': 'Climate change refers to long-term shifts in temperatures and weather patterns. Although some climate variations occur naturally, human activities have been the main driver of climate change since the 1800s, mainly through the burning of fossil fuels such as coal, oil, and gas.'}, {'title': 'NASA is a global leader in studying Earth’s changing climate.', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'What are the effects of climate change? The effects of human-caused global warming are happening now, are irreversible for people alive today, and will worsen as long as humans add greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.'}, {'title': 'Causes of Climate Change | US EPA', 'url': 'https://www.epa.gov/climatechange-science/causes-climate-change', 'snippet': 'Burning fossil fuels changes the climate more than any other human activity.Causes of Climate Change. Natural processes are always influencing the earth’s climate and can explain climate changes prior to the Industrial Revolution in the 1700s.'}, {'title': 'What are the effects of global warming? | National Geographic', 'url': 'https://www.nationalgeographic.com/environment/article/global-warming-effects', 'snippet': 'Global warming and climate change are often used interchangeably as synonyms, but scientists prefer to use “climate change” when describing the complex shifts now affecting our planet’s weather and climate systems.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 10.281474900024477}
{'query': 'global average temperatures trend 2023 2024 latest data NASA NOAA', 'results': [{'title': 'Climate change: global temperature | NOAA Climate.gov', 'url': 'https://www.climate.gov/news-features/understanding-climate/climate-change-global-temperature', 'snippet': 'Global temperatures in 2024 were above the 1991-2020 average (red) across most of the planet. Yearly temperatures compared to the 20th-century average (bar chart) show that it has been 48 years since Earth had a cooler-than-average year. NOAA Climate.gov image, based on data...'}, {'title': 'Global Temperature - Earth Indicator - NASA Science', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/earth/explore/earth-indicators/global-temperature/', 'snippet': 'Global temperatures in 2025 were cooler than 2024, with average temperatures of 2.14 degrees Fahrenheit (1.19 degrees Celsius) above the 1951 to 1980 average. The data shown are the latest available, updated annually.'}, {'title': 'NASA Confirms: Every Month For Last Year Was Hottest on Record', 'url': 'https://www.pinterest.com/pin/nasa-confirms-every-month-for-last-year-was-hottest-on-record--281967626663435617/', 'snippet': 'Global temperature trends shows the past 12 months of monthly temperature records. This continues a warming trend that has been growing for the past decade. The NASA data also shows the yearly global temperatures during the past 10 years have been the warmest on record.'}, {'title': 'NOAA winter 2023-24 forecast: How cold will it be? What about El Nin o?', 'url': 'https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/weather/2023/10/19/noaa-winter-forecast-cold-temperatures/71214343007/', 'snippet': "NOAA winter 2023-2024 forecast: Here's where it's expected to be unusually warm this year.Warmer-than-average temperatures are favored across the northern tier of the U.S. and much of the far West, NOAA said."}, {'title': 'Planetary K-index | NOAA / NWS Space Weather Prediction Center', 'url': 'https://www.spaceweather.gov/products/planetary-k-index', 'snippet': 'The Estimated 3-hour Planetary Kp-index is derived at the NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center using data from the following ground-based magnetometers: Sitka, Alaska; Meanook, Canada; Ottawa, Canada; Fredericksburg, Virginia; Hartland, UK; Wingst, Germany; Niemegk, Germany...'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 6.104698600014672}
